  "report_markdown": "# Cap Table \u2014 Acmecorp Inc.\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nModeled 2 scenario(s) for Acmecorp Inc.: 2 full, 0 mixed, 0 repay-only, 0 pending input.\n1 counsel-review item(s) surfaced. 14 date-sensitive item(s) in watchlist.\nFounder ownership ranges 70.0% to 72.0% across resolved scenarios.\n\n## Current Cap State\n\nAs of: 2026-06-23\n\n| Holder | Shares (as-converted) | % of FD |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Founder A | 5,000,000 | 45.0% |\n| Founder B | 5,000,000 | 45.0% |\n| Options available | 1,111,111 | 10.0% |\n| **Total fully-diluted** | **11,111,111** | **100.0%** |\n\n## Scenarios Modeled\n\n### Series A \u2013 as written (no pool top-up) (Priced round)\n\n**Stage:** Fully modeled (`full`)\n\n**Inputs:**\n- `pre_money`: 20000000\n- `new_money`: 5000000\n\n**Post-round ownership:**\n- founders pct: 72.0%\n- preferred pct: 0.0%\n- option pool pct: 8.0%\n- safe pct: 0.0%\n- note pct: 0.0%\n- new money pct: 20.0%\n\n**Equity financing price:** $1.8000/share\n\n**Founder Impact Lens:** Founders collectively held 90.0% of fully-diluted shares before this scenario; after, 72.0%. That's -18.0 percentage points.\n\n_Provenance: rules: `safe.post_money_cap_conversion`_\n\n### Series A \u2013 with 10% post-money pool top-up (Priced round)\n\n**Stage:** Fully modeled (`full`)\n\n**Inputs:**\n- `pre_money`: 20000000\n- `new_money`: 5000000\n- `target_pool_percent`: 0.1\n- `target_basis`: post_money\n\n**Post-round ownership:**\n- founders pct: 70.0%\n- preferred pct: 0.0%\n- option pool pct: 10.0%\n- safe pct: 0.0%\n- note pct: 0.0%\n- new money pct: 20.0%\n\n**Equity financing price:** $1.7500/share\n\n**Founder Impact Lens:** Founders collectively held 90.0% of fully-diluted shares before this scenario; after, 70.0%. That's -20.0 percentage points.\n\n_Provenance: rules: `safe.post_money_cap_conversion`_\n\n## Scenario Comparison\n\n| Scenario | Stage | Founder %  | Equity Price |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Series A \u2013 as written (no pool top-up) | Fully modeled | 72.0% | $1.8000 |\n| Series A \u2013 with 10% post-money pool top-up | Fully modeled | 70.0% | $1.7500 |\n\n## Counsel Review Required\n\n### Delaware Cross Border\n- **[QSBS rules are date-sensitive](https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2025/dec/revisiting-sec-1202-strategic-planning-after-the-2025-obbba-expansion/)** (`delaware_cross_border.qsbs_date_sensitive`)\n  - US QSBS eligibility and exclusion amounts are date-sensitive and changed for stock issued after July 4, 2025 under OBBBA; cap-table scripts should flag issue date and tax counsel review.\n\n## Date-Sensitive Watchlist\n\n_14 rule(s) to watch (from 14 matched instances)._\n\n| Rule | Status | When | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Cross-border IP and transfer pricing](https://kpmg.com/us/en/taxnewsflash/news/2025/11/israel-final-guidance-local-r-and-d-centers-ip-valuations.html) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the tax position date for this instance. |\n| [Israel 2025 SAFE temporary guidance](https://www.gov.il/BlobFolder/policy/procedures-290125/he/IncomeTax_procedures-290125.pdf) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the safe investment date for this instance. |\n| [Israeli Registrar online reporting](https://barlaw.co.il/practice_areas/corporate/client_updates/compulsory-online-reporting-to-the-israeli-registrar-of-companies/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the filing date for this instance. |\n| [Israeli flip ruling path is not one-size-fits-all](https://arnontl.com/news/significant-tax-reliefs-in-corporate-restructuring-amendment-to-the-israeli-income-tax-ordinance/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the restructuring approval date for this instance. |\n| [May 2025 Israeli restructuring changes](https://arnontl.com/news/significant-tax-reliefs-in-corporate-restructuring-amendment-to-the-israeli-income-tax-ordinance/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the restructuring effective date for this instance. |\n| [Non-qualifying Israeli SAFE facts-and-circumstances review](https://www.gov.il/BlobFolder/policy/procedures-290125/he/IncomeTax_procedures-290125.pdf) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the safe investment date for this instance. |\n| [Options, SAFEs, and notes in a flip](https://www.pearlcohen.com/section-102-options-the-unwritten-rules-and-pitfalls-to-look-for/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the flip closing date for this instance. |\n| [QSBS rules are date-sensitive](https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2025/dec/revisiting-sec-1202-strategic-planning-after-the-2025-obbba-expansion/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the stock issue date for this instance. |\n| [Section 102 capital-gains track checklist](https://www.icnl.org/wp-content/uploads/Israel_Ordinance.pdf) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the grant date for this instance. |\n| [Section 102 double-trigger acceleration treatment](https://www.shibolet.com/en/double-trigger-acceleration-upon-exit-or-ipo/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the transaction event date for this instance. |\n| [Section 102 plan-design pitfalls](https://www.pearlcohen.com/section-102-options-the-unwritten-rules-and-pitfalls-to-look-for/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the grant date for this instance. |\n| [Section 102 treatment for foreign parent shares](https://www.icnl.org/wp-content/uploads/Israel_Ordinance.pdf) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the grant date for this instance. |\n| [Section 3(i) nonemployee equity](https://www.icnl.org/wp-content/uploads/Israel_Ordinance.pdf) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the grant date for this instance. |\n| [Qualified financing threshold and automatic conversion](https://www.cooleygo.com/convertible-debt/) | unknown | \u2014 | Set a benchmark reference date in your inputs to use current data. |\n\n## Sources Cited\n\n- `TAXADVISER-QSBS-OBBBA`\n\n---\n\n<!-- COACHING_INSERTION_POINT_9af5f881 -->\n\n---\n\n*Generated by [founder skills](htt